      "tag": "SATB",
      "h2": "Four Voice Types",
      "body_html": "<p>The four standard voices are <strong>S</strong>oprano, <strong>A</strong>lto, <strong>T</strong>enor, <strong>B</strong>ass — <strong>SATB</strong>. Choirs are written in 4 parts, one per voice.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Boys",
      "h2": "Voice Breaking",
      "body_html": "<p>Boys' voices typically drop around age 12-14 (puberty). A boy soprano (treble) may become a tenor or bass. Some keep a high <strong>countertenor</strong> range.</p>"
    },
